4.2 Chess Game Setup Methods
Class	Java signature	What it does
Game	void startNewGame()	Creates a fresh Board, sets up the pieces, and sets the active color to WHITE.
Game	Board getBoard()	Returns the current board so the GUI can display it.
Game	Color getActiveColor()	Returns the color whose turn it is.
Board	void setupStartingPosition()	Places all 32 pieces on their starting squares on a fresh board.
Board	Piece getPieceAt(int row, int col)	Returns the piece on the given square, or null if it’s empty.
Piece	Piece(PieceType type, Color color)	Constructor that creates a piece with a type and color.
Piece	PieceType getType()	Returns the kind of piece, such as KNIGHT.
Piece	Color getColor()	Returns the piece’s color, WHITE or BLACK.
GUI	void handleNewGame()	Handles the New Game click by starting the game, rendering the board, and updating the turn label.
GUI	void renderBoard(Board board)	Reads all 64 squares and displays the appropriate piece icon or an empty square.
GUI	void updateTurnLabel(Color activeColor)	Updates the label to show whose turn it is.
